<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">raise-vampire</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Raise Vampire</ansi> spell performs the forbidden rite that transforms a
worthy corpse into a blood-drinking undead noble. Unlike lesser risen, the
vampire retains cunning and can act with terrifying independence. Only the
most formidable remains can survive the dark gift's demands.

Vampires are predatory spellcasters that drain the lifeforce from their foes
through both claw and sorcery. They heal themselves by wounding others,
making them dangerous foes that grow stronger as battle rages.

The servant's power scales with your Charisma and manifestation skill, and
with the remains you raise it from. Part of it is drawn from the corpse, so
the same spell over better remains yields a better servant. A vampire is a
demanding thing to keep, second only to a flesh golem.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast raise-vampire [corpse]</ansi>     Animate nearby remains.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> Extended channel
<ansi fg="yellow">Corpse:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Requires immense remains</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Nearby corpse or ground loot</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Cast Cost:   </ansi> Notable, and paid only once
<ansi fg="yellow">Held Cost:   </ansi> Notable, for as long as you keep it
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Manifestation</ansi>

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - The vampire appears under your command and aids you in combat.
  - Once raised, the undead servant remains active as a companion.
  - Use the <ansi fg="command">assess</ansi> command to evaluate a corpse's quality.
  - Raising costs conviction once. Keeping the servant sets conviction
    aside for as long as it walks with you, and that held share, not
    the casting price, is what limits how many you can field.
  - A mightier servant holds more of your will, and better remains
    make a mightier servant.
  - Skill in manifestation lowers what a companion holds, so practice
    buys you a larger following as well as a stronger one.
  - If your conviction is already spoken for, the raising is refused
    outright rather than leaving you weaker, and costs you nothing.

